WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.283
A compact wheel loader is due for service.

00:00:03.283 --> 00:00:07.280
Its owner needs an air filter, and doesn't have the part number.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:13.357
Spark puts Parts Intelligence and ordering in one conversation.

00:00:13.357 --> 00:00:17.040
Start with the machine, the part or the job at hand.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:23.110
Ask for an air filter for the NV-3200, preferably in stock.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:31.997
Spark checks fitment, catalogue status and stock, and recommends one part: it fits, it is verified, and it is in stock.

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:34.960
It also says what it left out, and why.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.329
Ask to see it as a graph.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:47.208
Parts Intelligence draws the recorded relationships: the three machines it fits, its two suppliers, and the six depots that hold it.

00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:51.280
Every link is marked as source data, or synthetic demo data.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.268
Then say: order it.

00:00:54.268 --> 00:01:03.350
Spark fills the order from the saved profile, with the delivery site, dealer and contact, and proposes the fastest recorded delivery.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.841
Want a different delivery?

00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:13.521
Spark compares the recorded options by depot, arrival estimate and total cost, best match first.

00:01:13.521 --> 00:01:16.620
Standard road arrives a day later, for less.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.917
Every change updates the same order.

00:01:20.917 --> 00:01:26.617
The review shows the part, delivery, dealer, contact and total, excluding VAT.

00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:30.080
Nothing is ordered until you press Place order.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:32.397
Find it.

00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:34.015
See how it connects.

00:01:34.015 --> 00:01:35.942
Order it, on your terms.

00:01:35.942 --> 00:01:37.560
Spark, at Noordveld.
